  "description": "PUTXAE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H98 Co6 Gd4 N12 O50 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),5(C1 H4 O1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.048-4.041 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.77-112.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII2CoIII4GdIII4(Htris)8(OAc)6(NO3)4(H2O)(MeOH)](NO3)2·5MeOH·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Co(III), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
